# Shell scripts keep LF line endings on every checkout, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF on checkout. Bash reads the trailing \r as part of each line, so a CRLF
# script dies on its first real statement:
#   line 6: $'\r': command not found
#   line 7: set: pipefail: invalid option name
# That broke every `bash scripts/*.sh` gate and all three git hooks for anyone
# contributing from Windows, and it would ship CRLF in the terminal's shell
# integration files. `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf per path, so these stay LF
# whatever the local git config says.
#
# scripts/shell-script-eol.test.mjs fails if a tracked shell script (found by
# extension OR by shebang) is not covered here.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.zsh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Agent-journal golden fixtures are byte-exact: the Rust provenance suites
# compare serialized layouts against them line by line, and a CRLF checkout
# fails every comparison (CI's Windows leg did). `golden_text` in
# src-tauri/src/agent_journal/test_golden_prov.test.rs asserts no CR survives.
# Everything else keeps git's defaults.
src/test/fixtures/agentJournal/** text eol=lf
